  "verdict": "CLOSED, and by the Milnor invariant itself. The six local monodromies lift to only FOUR distinct braid words, two of which already generate: sigma_1 = g0^-1 and sigma_2^-1 = g0^-1 g1 g0. So the monodromy image is not a proper subgroup of B_3 — it IS B_3, and its pure part is all of P_3. The Borromean braid (sigma_1 sigma_2^-1)^3 is therefore an element of the image; built from the loop lifts it has every pairwise linking number zero (indeterminacy 0, so mu-bar is a genuine integer) and mu-bar_123 = -1, against 0 for the identity, which is also in the image. Both are pure, so both carry sign character +1. The two colour sign lines agree as sign characters and disagree on mu-bar, ON THIS FIBRATION — the vacuous-agreement escape of F5 is closed on the very invariant the Milnor route locates colour antisymmetry in, not merely on a lower one.",
  "scope_note": "The verdict is now a PROOF of group membership plus an exact integer computation, not a sample, so it is not scope-(a): the image equals B_3 by exhibiting both Artin generators as words in the loop lifts, and mu-bar_123 = -1 on an element of it. What remains conditional is the INPUT — the six loop words come from bring_monodromy_braid_lift_probe's numerical continuation, guarded but numerical. If those words are right, this conclusion is exact.",
  "superseded_scope": "Scope-(a) either way: this reads the six local monodromies lifted by bring_monodromy_braid_lift_probe and their pairwise products, not the whole image group. A zero here bounds what these words show, and excludes nothing about the image.",
